      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "retry",
      "heading": "Retry",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "what-is-retry",
      "heading": "What is Retry?",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Retry is used for transient exceptions—errors that may succeed after a few attempts."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Examples:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Concurrency conflict",
            "Temporary DB lock",
            "Network hiccup"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Retry is expensive because each retry triggers a rollback."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 30,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "xml-example",
      "heading": "XML Example",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "xml",
          "code": "<tasklet>\n    <chunk reader=\"reader\" writer=\"writer\" commit-interval=\"100\" retry-limit=\"3\">\n        <retryable-exception-classes>\n            <include class=\"org.springframework.dao.OptimisticLockingFailureException\"/>\n        </retryable-exception-classes>\n    </chunk>\n</tasklet>",
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "java-config-example",
      "heading": "Java Config Example",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "java",
          "code": ".faultTolerant()\n.retry(OptimisticLockingFailureException.class)\n.retryLimit(3)",
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "combining-retry-and-skip",
      "heading": "Combining Retry and Skip",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "why-combine-them",
      "heading": "Why combine them?",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Some errors are:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Transient (retry first)",
            "But if still failing → skip the item instead of failing the job."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Workflow:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": true,
          "items": [
            "Retry up to retry-limit",
            "If still failing → skip the problematic item",
            "Fail the job only if skip-limit is exceeded"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 40,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "xml-example",
      "heading": "XML Example",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "xml",
          "code": "<tasklet>\n    <chunk reader=\"reader\" writer=\"writer\"\n           commit-interval=\"100\"\n           retry-limit=\"3\"\n           skip-limit=\"10\">\n\n        <retryable-exception-classes>\n            <include class=\"org.springframework.dao.DeadlockLoserDataAccessException\"/>\n        </retryable-exception-classes>\n\n        <skippable-exception-classes>\n            <include class=\"org.springframework.dao.DeadlockLoserDataAccessException\"/>\n        </skippable-exception-classes>\n\n    </chunk>\n</tasklet>",
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "java-config-example",
      "heading": "Java Config Example",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "java",
          "code": ".faultTolerant()\n.retry(DeadlockLoserDataAccessException.class)\n.retryLimit(3)\n.skip(DeadlockLoserDataAccessException.class)\n.skipLimit(10)",
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "restart",
      "heading": "Restart",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "what-is-restart",
      "heading": "What is Restart?",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Restart enables a failed job to resume exactly from where it left off, using metadata stored in a persistent repository."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 20,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "requirements",
          "heading": "Requirements",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "A persistent JobRepository (JDBC)",
                "The job must have previously failed",
                "Restartable is enabled by default"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 15,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "important-attributes",
      "heading": "Important Attributes",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Attribute",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "restartable (job attribute)",
              "Turn restart on/off"
            ],
            [
              "allow-start-if-complete (tasklet)",
              "Allow rerunning a completed step"
            ],
            [
              "start-limit (tasklet)",
              "Limit number of times a step can restart"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 25,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "xml-example",
      "heading": "XML Example",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "xml",
          "code": "<job id=\"fileJob\" restartable=\"true\">\n    <step id=\"decompress\" next=\"readWriteItems\">\n        <tasklet allow-start-if-complete=\"true\">\n            ...\n        </tasklet>\n    </step>\n\n    <step id=\"readWriteItems\" next=\"cleanUp\">\n        <tasklet start-limit=\"3\">\n            ...\n        </tasklet>\n    </step>\n</job>",
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 0,
